{
  "statement": "The SafetyAgent emphasizes the critical importance of safety and reliability in the ATM system. SAF-01 ensures that accounts do not incur negative balances, protecting users from financial distress. SAF-02 and SAF-03 work together to facilitate safe transactions, automatically withdrawing from savings when necessary and informing users of insufficient funds. SAF-04 logs all transactions for accountability, while SAF-05 secures user authentication through PIN verification. Additionally, SAF-06 allows safe degradation, enabling limited withdrawals during maintenance, and SAF-07 ensures users are informed about their account status post-transaction. All these requirements are essential to maintain user trust and operational safety.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["RES-03", "TRU-04"],
      "type": "redundant",
      "description": "Both RES-03 and TRU-04 aim to prevent negative balances, overlapping with SAF-01."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-02", "EFF-05"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "SAF-02's automatic withdrawal may conflict with EFF-05's requirement for user delay when funds are insufficient."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-03", "RES-06"],
      "type": "redundant",
      "description": "Both SAF-03 and RES-06 address notifying users of insufficient funds, leading to redundancy."
    }
  ],
